# 9Router Model Inventory + Sync Cron — Every 3 Days
# =====================================================
# Install: sudo cp cron-9router-sync /etc/cron.d/9router-sync
# Or user crontab: crontab -e  → paste the line below
# (requires cron daemon running: sudo systemctl enable --now cron)

# Runs every 3 days at 03:30 UTC (adjust time as needed)
# Model inventory runs first (~15-30 min), then sync runs (~5-15 min)
# Logs: executions/9router/logs/<timestamp>-model-inventory-cron.log
#       executions/9router/logs/<timestamp>-9router-sync-cron.log

# System-wide (needs root):
# 30 3 */3 * * root /home/coder/sysops-playbooks/playbooks/9router/scripts/model-inventory-cron.sh >> /var/log/model-inventory-cron.log 2>&1
# 45 3 */3 * * root /home/coder/sysops-playbooks/playbooks/9router/scripts/9router-sync-cron.sh >> /var/log/9router-sync-cron.log 2>&1

# User crontab (no root):
# 30 3 */3 * * /home/coder/sysops-playbooks/playbooks/9router/scripts/model-inventory-cron.sh >> ~/model-inventory-cron.log 2>&1
# 45 3 */3 * * /home/coder/sysops-playbooks/playbooks/9router/scripts/9router-sync-cron.sh >> ~/9router-sync-cron.log 2>&1

# Alternative: systemd timer (recommended for servers)
# See templates/systemd-9router-sync.{service,timer}
# Install:
#   sudo cp templates/systemd-9router-sync.service /etc/systemd/system/
#   sudo cp templates/systemd-9router-sync.timer /etc/systemd/system/
#   sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl enable --now 9router-sync.timer
# Timer runs every 3 days (OnCalendar=*-*-*/3 03:30)

# Environment for cron (user crontab needs these):
# REPO_ROOT=/home/coder/sysops-playbooks
# PYTHON_BIN=/home/coder/sysops-playbooks/.venv/bin/python
# NINEROUTER_URL=https://router.munyard.biz
# AA_API_KEY=...  (optional, for Artificial Analysis intelligence scores)
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...
# OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY=...
# OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY=...
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=...
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=...
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...
# COMMAND_CODE_API_KEY=...

# Note: The scripts auto-discover the execution variant (executions/9router/ or
# executions/9router-<suffix>/) and use its config/secrets. No config args needed.